# Reachable Go vulnerabilities accepted by the CI audit (ci-templates' Go preset).
# Format: GO-YYYY-NNNN  # why the vulnerable code is not exposed
# Every entry needs a reason; anything reachable that isn't listed still fails the
# audit, and entries no longer reported raise a warning to remove them.
#
# grafana/tempo (#6): whole-module advisories (no affected symbols), so govulncheck
# flags any use of the module. Their only fixes are tempo v2.x releases; tempo is a
# v1-path Go module (no /v2), so no fixed Go module version exists. We import only
# github.com/grafana/tempo/pkg/traceql, the TraceQL parser (enforcer_traceql.go);
# the advisories concern tempo's server components, which are neither imported nor
# run here. Also accepted in .trivyignore. Reassess if we import tempo server or
# storage packages, or when tempo publishes a /v2 module path.
